From 90a3e22a56ec6b3eb43a4cce996f18ab51aaa590 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Beri <jmberi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 22:27:37 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] boards: waveshare: add ESP32-P4-Module-DEV-KIT

Add board support for the Waveshare ESP32-P4-Module-DEV-KIT, a Raspberry Pi
Model B sized ESP32-P4 board built on the ESP32-P4-Module (32 MB PSRAM,
16 MB flash, v1.3 silicon). HP and LP core targets, MCUboot sysbuild.

Enabled: UART0 console on the CH343P port (tx=37, rx=38), I2C0, I2S0 for
the ES8311 codec, the MicroSD slot, 100M Ethernet behind an IP101GR, and
the MIPI DSI display the DEV-KIT-C ships with -- a JD9365 800x1280 panel
with a GT911 touch controller.

Peripheral wiring is shared with the ESP32-P4-WIFI6-Dev-Kit this is derived
from, and was checked against the board schematic and against the pins the
board's own ESP-IDF factory firmware prints at boot.

Two things differ from the Espressif Function EV board and are easy to get
wrong. The panel's FPC carries no reset, backlight or touch interrupt line:
reset and backlight are registers on the panel board's MCU at 0x45, and the
GT911 is polled. GPIO26 and GPIO27, which the EV board uses for panel reset
and backlight, are 40-pin header I/O here and reach nothing.

The ESP32-C6 is on SDIO rather than SPI, so Zephyr's esp_hosted driver
cannot drive it; the wiring is recorded but wireless is not available.

Signed-off-by: Jonathan Beri <jmberi@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
