--- /dev/null
+++ b/boards/waveshare/esp32p4_module_dev_kit/doc/index.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,98 @@
+.. zephyr:board:: esp32p4_module_dev_kit
+
+Overview
+********
+
+The Waveshare ESP32-P4-Module-DEV-KIT is a Raspberry Pi Model B sized
+multimedia board built around the ESP32-P4-Module, which packages an
+ESP32-P4NRW32 with 32 MB of stacked PSRAM and 16 MB of NOR flash. It carries
+wired connectivity (USB, 100M Ethernet with PoE header, MicroSD), audio,
+MIPI CSI/DSI connectors and a 40-pin GPIO header. Wireless comes from an
+on-board ESP32-C6 reached over SDIO.
+
+This board definition provides both high-performance (HP) core and low-power
+(LP) core targets.
+
+Hardware
+********
+
+The board included peripherals:
+
+- ESP32-P4-Module (silicon revision v1.3) with 32 MB stacked PSRAM in HEX
+  mode and 16 MB on-module NOR flash
+- Type-C USB-to-UART port (CH343P) for power, flashing and the serial
+  console, wired to UART0 (tx=GPIO37, rx=GPIO38)
+- Type-A USB OTG 2.0 HS port behind a CH334F hub, host/device switchable
+  via jumper
+- 100M Ethernet RJ45 with an IC+ IP101GR PHY (RMII: clk=50, tx_en=49,
+  txd0=34, txd1=35, crs_dv=28, rxd0=29, rxd1=30; SMI: mdc=31, mdio=52;
+  reset=GPIO51, PHY address 1), with a PoE module header
+- ES8311 audio codec on I2S0 (mclk=13, bclk=12, ws=10, din=11, dout=9) with
+  a speaker PA enabled by GPIO53, and an on-board microphone
+- MicroSD slot (4-bit SDHC at 40 MHz: clk=43, cmd=44, d0=39, d1=40, d2=41,
+  d3=42) powered through a GPIO45 load switch
+- I2C0 (sda=GPIO7, scl=GPIO8), shared by the audio codec and both the CSI
+  and DSI connectors; separate I2C and I3C headers
+- 2-lane MIPI DSI display connector and 2-lane MIPI CSI camera connector
+- RTC battery holder (rechargeable batteries only)
+- 40-pin GPIO expansion header, boot and reset buttons
+
+Display
+=======
+
+The DEV-KIT-C variant ships with the Waveshare 10.1in DSI touch panel, and
+the board devicetree enables it: a Jadard JD9365 at 800x1280 over two lanes,
+with a Goodix GT911 touch controller at 0x5D on the shared I2C bus.
+
+Two things about that panel are worth knowing before wiring anything else to
+it. Its 22-pin FPC carries only 3V3, I2C and the MIPI lanes, so **there is no
+reset, backlight or touch-interrupt line**: panel reset and backlight are
+register writes to the panel board's own MCU at I2C address 0x45, and the
+GT911 has to be polled, which is why ``CONFIG_INPUT_GT911_INTERRUPT`` is
+defaulted off here. The panel also draws its backlight power from a
+**separate 2-pin 5V connector** that has to be plugged in as well as the FPC.
+
+Do not copy the ESP32-P4-Function-EV-Board's ``reset-gpios``/``bl-gpios`` for
+this panel. GPIO26 and GPIO27 are 40-pin header I/O on this board and are not
+connected to the display.
+
+The panel is natively portrait and the JD9365 has no transpose bit, so
+``display_set_orientation()`` accepts only ``DISPLAY_ORIENTATION_NORMAL``.
+
+Wireless
+========
+
+The ESP32-C6 co-processor is wired over SDIO (clk=18, cmd=19, d0-d3=14-17,
+with the C6 held in reset by GPIO54). Zephyr's ``esp_hosted`` driver is
+SPI-only, so there is nothing to bind to it yet and Wi-Fi and Bluetooth are
+not available. The wiring is recorded in the devicetree for whoever adds it.
+
+.. include:: ../../../espressif/common/soc-esp32p4-features.rst
+   :start-after: espressif-soc-esp32p4-features
